  <!-- API Reference: Webhooks -->
  <section id="api-webhooks">
    <h2>Webhooks</h2>
    <p>Receive events from external services via webhook bots.</p>

    <h3>Webhook Endpoint</h3>
    <pre class="docs-code">POST /api/v1/webhooks/{webhook_id}</pre>

    <h3>Request Headers</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Header</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>Content-Type</code></td><td>Yes</td><td><code>application/json</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>X-Hub-Signature-256</code></td><td>Yes</td><td>HMAC-SHA256 signature of the request body</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Signature Verification</h3>
    <p>To verify a webhook request:</p>
    <pre class="docs-code"># Ruby example
expected = "sha256=" + OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest(
  "SHA256",
  webhook_secret,
  request.raw_post
)

if expected == request.headers["X-Hub-Signature-256"]
  # Request is authentic
end</pre>

    <h3>Supported Actions</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Action</th><th>Description</th><th>Required Fields</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>send_message</code></td><td>Post a message to a channel</td><td><code>channel_id</code>, <code>content</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>status_update</code></td><td>Update bot status</td><td><code>status</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- API Reference: Home Assistant -->
  <section id="home-assistant">
    <h2>Home Assistant Integration</h2>
    <p>HomeChat integrates seamlessly with Home Assistant for smart home automation.</p>

    <h3>Installation</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Copy the <code>homechat</code> custom component to your Home Assistant config:
        <pre class="docs-code">&lt;ha_config&gt;/custom_components/homechat/</pre>
      </li>
      <li>Create an API token in HomeChat Admin > Automations > API Tokens</li>
      <li>Add the configuration to your <code>configuration.yaml</code>:
        <pre class="docs-code">homechat:
  host: your-homechat-server
  port: 3000
  ssl: false
  token: your_api_token</pre>
      </li>
      <li>Restart Home Assistant</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Server Discovery</h3>
    <p>HomeChat advertises its capabilities via the server info endpoint:</p>
    <pre class="docs-code">GET /api/v1/server_info

{
  "name": "HomeChat",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "mode": "local",
  "capabilities": ["chat", "api", "webhooks", "realtime"],
  "push_enabled": true,
  "registration_enabled": true
}</pre>

    <h3>Home Assistant Add-on Mode</h3>
    <p>When running as a Home Assistant add-on, HomeChat automatically:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Detects the HA environment</li>
      <li>Configures ingress support</li>
      <li>Integrates with Nabu Casa (if available)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Set the <code>HOME_ASSISTANT_ADDON=true</code> environment variable to enable add-on mode.</p>

    <h3>Real-time Updates</h3>
    <p>HomeChat uses WebSocket for real-time communication:</p>
    <pre class="docs-code">WebSocket URL: wss://your-server/cable</pre>
    <p>Subscribe to channels to receive real-time message updates in your Home Assistant automations.</p>
  </section>

